<title>INDIA: India RBI buys dollars to arrest rupee's rise.</title>
<headline>India RBI buys dollars to arrest rupee's rise.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) on Wednesday bought dollars at the rate of 35.705/710 rupees to stem the rupee's rise, dealers said.  </p>
<p>&quot;They bought between 35.705 and 35.710,&quot; a dealer at a city bank said. He said the RBI stepped in after the rupee threatened to breach the 35.70-mark.</p>
<p>The rupee was quoted at 35.710/715 in latest deals, after opening Wednesday steady at 35.70/71 to the dollar.</p>
<p>The central bank has been buying dollars throughout this week as the rupee tested the 35.70 mark, dealers said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
